{
  "title": "IDURAR ERP CRM \u2014 ecommerce (8,413\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: IDURAR ERP CRM\nDomain: ecommerce | Scale: medium | Stars: 8,413\nProblem: Small to medium businesses need an affordable, self-hostable ERP and CRM solution for managing invoices, quotes, payments, and customer relationships. IDURAR provides a free, open-source alternative to expensive commercial ERP/CRM platforms.\nTarget users: small business owners, accountants, sales teams, freelancers, developers seeking a self-hosted ERP/CRM solution\nCore features: Invoice Management; Quote/Estimate Management; Payment Management; Customer (CRM) Management; Accounting Module; Inventory Management; HR Management\nIntegrations: MongoDB Atlas, DigitalOcean\nTech stack: React.js with Ant Design (AntD) and Redux + Node.js with Express.js + MongoDB with Mongoose + Self-hosted / DigitalOcean (cloud.idurarapp.com)\nKey libraries: React, Redux, Ant Design, Express.js, Mongoose, Pug\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Uses the MERN stack (MongoDB, Express, React, Node) as a full-stack JavaScript monolith, reducing context-switching and simplifying deployment for self-hosted scenarios.\n- Adopts Ant Design as the UI component framework, accelerating development of data-dense ERP interfaces like tables, forms, and dashboards.\n- Redux is used for global state management on the frontend, a common pattern for complex business applications with shared state across many views.\n- Released under AGPL-3.0 ('Fair-Code') while offering a paid cloud-hosted enterprise version, demonstrating an open-core monetization strategy.",
